WEBVTT

00:16.683 --> 00:18.560
Thanks for waiting.

00:18.643 --> 00:21.271
Here's your chicken katsu
and stewed fish meal.

00:21.354 --> 00:22.647
Check please.

00:22.731 --> 00:23.815
Okay.

00:31.990 --> 00:34.367
-Excuse me. Can you take my order?
-Yes.

00:34.993 --> 00:36.494
Welcome.

00:48.214 --> 00:49.966
Now I just save this…

00:52.927 --> 00:54.387
Texture… Texture…

00:56.765 --> 00:58.349
Oh crap!

00:59.476 --> 01:00.602
-Sorry, Shige.
-What?

01:00.685 --> 01:04.773
For the family at table one,
their child can't eat seafood.

01:05.482 --> 01:08.526
Oh really?
We just ran out of ginger pork, right?

01:08.610 --> 01:09.736
Yes.

01:11.571 --> 01:14.491
Think of something we can make
with the ingredients we have left.

01:14.574 --> 01:15.909
Okay.

01:26.920 --> 01:30.590
We can make Japanese-style Hamburg Steak
using leftover gyoza filling.

01:31.549 --> 01:34.219
-Sounds good. Can you do that?
-Yes.

01:37.972 --> 01:39.140
Excuse me.

01:39.224 --> 01:42.101
Will your daughter be all right
with Japanese-style Hamburg Steak?

01:42.185 --> 01:43.019
‎Yes.

02:15.677 --> 02:17.053
NEW FOLDER - UPLOAD FILE

02:17.887 --> 02:19.055
UPLOAD

02:19.139 --> 02:21.933
UPLOADING PRACTICE ASSIGNMENT PARK RIN

02:22.016 --> 02:23.101
UPLOAD COMPLETE

02:24.978 --> 02:26.187
I'm done!

02:33.278 --> 02:36.698
STUDENT AFFAIRS
DORM ROOM 201 - TERMINATION INFORMATION

02:41.161 --> 02:42.370
Taiga.

02:43.872 --> 02:45.165
I'll bring the sign in.

02:46.082 --> 02:48.918
We need to think about our
new seasonal menu soon.

02:49.460 --> 02:51.296
Can't wait to see what it'll be.

02:52.630 --> 02:53.506
Want to do it?

02:55.258 --> 02:57.677
Huh? Me?

02:58.678 --> 03:00.263
You've been here three years already.

03:04.642 --> 03:08.021
-Thank you. I will give it a try.
-Okay.

03:08.813 --> 03:11.482
TANOMI

03:28.708 --> 03:29.626
OPEN

03:29.709 --> 03:33.129
CLOSED

04:36.025 --> 04:39.404
Huh? What do you mean
I have to move out by May?

04:40.113 --> 04:44.659
The dormitory you are currently living in,
is going to be temporarily closed

04:44.742 --> 04:47.495
for major renovation work
due to deterioration.

04:48.288 --> 04:49.664
Deterioration…?

04:49.747 --> 04:54.502
Well… We have been notifying everybody
about this for a while now.

04:55.128 --> 04:57.588
We also sent you a notice in the mail.

04:57.672 --> 04:58.506
‎SECOND WOMEN'S DORM

04:58.589 --> 05:00.466
Did you not receive that?

05:08.016 --> 05:10.435
Sorry… I found it.

05:11.227 --> 05:13.104
-Um…
-Yes?

05:13.187 --> 05:16.274
Do you know of any place where I can live?

05:17.108 --> 05:20.111
The raffle for the student apartments
has ended already, so…

05:20.778 --> 05:25.700
I believe you have no choice
but to find housing on your own.

05:40.339 --> 05:41.591
Thank you for the food.

05:53.978 --> 05:55.229
THE KIDS WANT TO COME OVER NEXT WEEK!

05:55.313 --> 05:56.355
SURE!

05:56.439 --> 05:57.523
CAN YOU SEND THE PHOTOS
FROM THE OTHER DAY?

05:57.607 --> 05:59.525
THE HASE FAMILY

06:15.666 --> 06:18.086
CLIENT INFORMATION SHEET - NAME: PARK RIN

06:18.169 --> 06:20.505
TOKYO UNIVERSITY OF FINE ARTS
SECOND WOMEN'S DORM ROOM 201

06:25.468 --> 06:27.220
Thank you.

06:29.055 --> 06:33.976
You're looking for a place that allows
immediate move-in and early termination?

06:34.060 --> 06:37.480
Yes. I need to move by next month.

06:38.481 --> 06:43.236
The choices are pretty limited
at this time of year…

06:44.570 --> 06:48.449
By the way, do you plan on staying
in Japan after graduation?

06:48.533 --> 06:49.826
What?

06:49.909 --> 06:52.453
If you don't have to terminate your lease
in less than a year,

06:52.537 --> 06:54.622
you will have a lot more options.

06:58.876 --> 06:59.961
I don't plan to.

07:01.045 --> 07:02.255
I see.

07:21.315 --> 07:24.861
You haven't captured the theme at all.

07:25.903 --> 07:27.530
The theme for this assignment

07:27.613 --> 07:30.867
was "the expression of unique textures,"
was it not?

07:31.451 --> 07:34.579
I do not see any thought
put into the textures.

07:35.746 --> 07:38.875
For example,
you could have shown how slimy it is,

07:38.958 --> 07:40.668
or crisp it is.

07:40.751 --> 07:44.255
You need to work on the expression,
and depiction of textures.

07:46.215 --> 07:47.175
Okay.

07:52.263 --> 07:53.556
Slimy…

07:55.349 --> 07:56.392
Slimy…

07:57.226 --> 07:59.520
Slimy? Slimy…

08:03.858 --> 08:05.985
Slimy…

08:06.068 --> 08:06.903
‎TRANSLATE
‎JAPANESE - KOREAN

08:10.490 --> 08:13.326
-Hello?
-Sorry for calling suddenly.

08:13.409 --> 08:16.287
About the property at Haibara Residence
that you were looking at…

08:16.370 --> 08:20.249
Another customer has just made
an appointment to take a tour of it.

08:21.334 --> 08:23.336
If you still want to apply for it,

08:23.419 --> 08:25.671
since you are of foreign nationality,

08:25.755 --> 08:28.341
you will need
your certificate of enrollment

08:28.925 --> 08:32.470
and a translated bank balance certificate.

08:41.020 --> 08:42.021
Hey.

08:44.315 --> 08:46.859
-He's Hase, my classmate from college.
-Welcome.

08:48.361 --> 08:52.198
He does have a toned, athletic build.
I can picture him running.

08:52.281 --> 08:56.536
He was so good that he was assigned to run
the first leg of the High School Ekiden.

08:56.619 --> 08:58.037
-Really?
-Right?

08:58.663 --> 09:02.083
Not only that, but in college
he ran alongside athletes

09:02.166 --> 09:04.085
like Kikuchi and Okubo.

09:04.168 --> 09:06.587
-That's amazing! They're so famous.
-Yeah!

09:06.671 --> 09:08.839
Do you still run now?

09:08.923 --> 09:10.841
No. That's all in the past.

09:10.925 --> 09:13.302
Hey! You should be more proud!

09:14.887 --> 09:17.139
Taiga, take the appetizers to table two.

09:17.223 --> 09:19.725
-Yes.
-What do you want to drink?

09:20.351 --> 09:21.644
Maybe bottled beer.

09:23.020 --> 09:24.939
Here is your certificate of enrollment.

09:25.773 --> 09:27.149
Thank you very much.

09:28.526 --> 09:29.819
Welcome.

09:40.454 --> 09:41.789
‎PARK

09:41.872 --> 09:45.334
-This please.
-Okay. It'll be about 30 minutes.

09:56.262 --> 10:00.975
PARK RIN

10:16.449 --> 10:20.328
Thank you very much.
That completes your application.

10:20.953 --> 10:24.248
I will contact you again,
once everything is reviewed.

10:24.957 --> 10:26.626
Thank you.

10:39.096 --> 10:40.640
I'm hungry…

10:45.978 --> 10:47.688
-Thanks for your work.
-Thank you.

10:47.772 --> 10:48.606
See you.

10:49.231 --> 10:50.775
Hey, Shige.

10:53.027 --> 10:55.112
Thank you for earlier.

11:06.582 --> 11:09.585
‎TANOMI

11:18.969 --> 11:21.555
I'm sorry, we're closed for today.

11:26.352 --> 11:27.895
Okay…

12:02.179 --> 12:05.224
MAMAMON

12:09.687 --> 12:12.731
You didn't know they were
remodeling the dorm?

12:13.566 --> 12:15.443
How can that even be?

12:17.194 --> 12:22.533
Well… I was really busy
with my assignment.

12:22.616 --> 12:25.911
What are you going to do
if you can't find a place to live?

12:26.787 --> 12:30.583
I know. It won't happen again.

12:30.666 --> 12:33.419
You know, when I ask about school,
you always say

12:33.502 --> 12:36.630
that you're doing fine.

12:36.714 --> 12:39.258
But are you really
keeping up with the class?

12:39.341 --> 12:41.385
All right, I get it!

12:43.012 --> 12:45.473
I'll do what I can
to find a place to live.

12:46.140 --> 12:47.016
Bye.

13:05.409 --> 13:08.829
TERMINATION NOTICE

13:20.382 --> 13:23.219
Joesongham-- I mean, I'm sorry.

13:24.428 --> 13:26.305
Um, are you hurt?

13:27.640 --> 13:29.225
Not at all.

13:29.767 --> 13:31.852
I'm really sorry.

13:31.936 --> 13:33.771
-Let me give you…
-It's fine.

13:39.443 --> 13:41.737
I'm really okay.

13:41.820 --> 13:43.906
No, please accept my apology.

13:44.615 --> 13:46.033
Give me your hand, please.

13:49.245 --> 13:50.412
Here.

13:54.708 --> 13:56.043
Thank you.

14:04.009 --> 14:05.636
Well… sorry about that…

14:07.471 --> 14:08.722
Wait…

14:32.121 --> 14:33.205
Enjoy.

14:35.791 --> 14:37.585
Thank you very much.

14:53.017 --> 14:54.184
It's good.

14:56.145 --> 14:59.732
Out of all the onigiri I've had in Japan,
this is the best.

15:01.525 --> 15:02.943
Thank you.

15:15.915 --> 15:17.124
Are you okay?

15:18.584 --> 15:21.754
Yeah… I just cut my finger earlier.

15:23.172 --> 15:24.506
Wait a second.

15:30.638 --> 15:31.472
‎Here.

15:35.059 --> 15:37.102
I cut my fingers a lot too, from cooking.

15:41.690 --> 15:43.317
Thank you.

15:52.076 --> 15:53.494
Have this too.

16:05.923 --> 16:07.549
This is amazing.

16:08.801 --> 16:10.427
What is this called?

16:10.511 --> 16:14.348
It's shigure-ni
with shishito peppers and beef.

16:15.265 --> 16:16.767
Shigure-ni…

16:18.143 --> 16:21.355
It tastes like Korean jang-jorim.

16:21.438 --> 16:23.148
Jang-jorim?

16:23.899 --> 16:25.693
How do you make that?

16:26.777 --> 16:30.572
I'm sorry, I don't know.

16:31.365 --> 16:33.450
I'm not good at cooking, actually.

16:35.327 --> 16:37.413
I'm good at eating, though.

16:50.759 --> 16:54.263
You eat like you really enjoy the food.

16:59.393 --> 17:00.227
‎Again?

17:01.103 --> 17:04.773
No, um… This is because…

17:05.983 --> 17:07.401
my stomach is stimulated.

17:10.946 --> 17:12.740
If I make more, will you eat it?

17:14.283 --> 17:15.451
Yes!

17:46.190 --> 17:48.150
Let me try this.

17:51.862 --> 17:52.988
That's sour!

17:54.656 --> 17:56.158
Tada!

18:03.290 --> 18:04.374
Shigure-ni, was it?

18:05.000 --> 18:07.961
That's what he stuffed it with.

18:09.088 --> 18:11.715
-Don't think about it.
-What?

18:13.008 --> 18:19.723
Park Rin, I have a massive database
of information from movies and dramas.

18:19.807 --> 18:21.225
And according to that,

18:21.308 --> 18:26.146
Japanese men are generally nice
to everyone by default.

18:26.230 --> 18:29.149
It's not because you're
particularly special.

18:31.902 --> 18:34.321
Didn't you used to live in Japan?

18:34.404 --> 18:36.240
Yeah, but I was in elementary school.

18:36.323 --> 18:38.450
Plus this isn't like that.

18:47.292 --> 18:49.336
I'm not going to date anyone.

18:49.419 --> 18:52.631
If my mom finds out,
she'll drag me back home immediately.

19:04.810 --> 19:06.520
The seasoning is totally different.

19:11.650 --> 19:13.277
It looks similar, though…

19:14.111 --> 19:17.114
JANG-JORIM

20:08.540 --> 20:09.750
Amazing…

20:10.792 --> 20:12.920
Truly a genius. A genius.

20:17.799 --> 20:18.967
I'm so jealous.

20:19.718 --> 20:23.013
If I had this kind of talent,
I bet I would have no worries.

20:29.353 --> 20:32.773
I see… Your mother is pretty mad, huh?

20:34.441 --> 20:38.987
I know. It's my fault.

20:39.613 --> 20:41.531
But when you're here, don't you sometimes

20:42.115 --> 20:45.035
feel like you've become so stupid?

20:46.536 --> 20:48.747
Things like checking the mail,

20:48.830 --> 20:50.958
and riding the bus…

20:51.041 --> 20:54.836
Things that I used to do normally
have suddenly become so difficult.

20:56.046 --> 20:59.007
‎If someone were to say,

20:59.091 --> 21:02.219
‎"That's the life you chose,"

21:03.011 --> 21:04.888
I'd have nothing to say back.

21:05.806 --> 21:06.682
But…

21:08.141 --> 21:09.810
I used to be a little more competent.

21:12.312 --> 21:13.563
What are you saying?

21:15.148 --> 21:16.108
Rin,

21:16.608 --> 21:18.360
you're very competent.

21:18.944 --> 21:20.445
You'll get through this soon.

21:20.529 --> 21:22.990
Trust me on this one.

21:24.574 --> 21:25.701
Okay?

21:26.910 --> 21:29.246
Okay. Thank you.

21:31.039 --> 21:34.126
I only have a year left,
so I'll try my best.

21:36.253 --> 21:38.630
Okay. You can talk to me anytime.

21:43.343 --> 21:45.137
You need to go back soon, right?

21:46.054 --> 21:47.389
What will you do for lunch?

21:48.473 --> 21:51.685
I'll just grab some onigiri.

21:57.232 --> 21:58.358
Hey,

21:58.900 --> 22:03.947
there's a good restaurant near the school.

22:05.073 --> 22:08.035
Do you want to go with me next time?

22:08.618 --> 22:10.662
-Want to go tonight?
-Really?

22:11.663 --> 22:14.124
I'd love that. Thank you.

22:15.250 --> 22:16.418
Shall we go?

22:21.506 --> 22:24.176
CLOSED

22:29.639 --> 22:32.017
‎JUN-HO - UGH, I'M TOO LAZY TO DO IT…

22:32.100 --> 22:33.852
SORRY THEY'RE CLOSED.
LET'S GO ANOTHER TIME.

22:33.935 --> 22:36.229
‎TANOMI

22:43.653 --> 22:48.241
I'm sorry. Today is our day off.

22:49.076 --> 22:51.495
Yeah, I just noticed.

22:54.498 --> 22:56.666
Well, I'll come again.

23:00.170 --> 23:03.590
Did you eat already?

23:06.676 --> 23:10.514
If you have time,
will you please give me your input?

23:11.306 --> 23:13.433
-Input?
-Yes.

23:13.975 --> 23:18.146
I'm thinking of doing a Korean-style dish
for our new menu item,

23:18.230 --> 23:19.397
but…

23:20.982 --> 23:22.943
it's not going so well.

23:23.026 --> 23:24.361
I'd appreciate your advice.

23:26.488 --> 23:27.572
Of course.

23:30.450 --> 23:33.078
Before that, may I ask you one thing?

23:33.745 --> 23:34.663
Yes?

23:35.789 --> 23:38.041
My name is Park Rin.

23:38.750 --> 23:39.709
What is your name?

23:42.170 --> 23:43.713
I'm Hase Taiga.

23:45.257 --> 23:47.425
I'll call you Taiga then.

23:53.515 --> 23:57.185
I want to use okra for its unique texture.

23:58.353 --> 24:00.355
It's my first time seeing

24:00.438 --> 24:01.690
-an okra.
-Huh?

24:02.274 --> 24:04.067
You don't eat okra in Korea?

24:05.402 --> 24:06.987
Do Koreans not like the slimy texture?

24:09.322 --> 24:10.365
Slimy!

24:11.366 --> 24:13.660
What does that mean?

24:13.743 --> 24:15.745
Let's see…

24:16.830 --> 24:17.873
Give me a second.

24:18.498 --> 24:19.666
All right…

24:34.556 --> 24:35.682
It's like this.

24:39.227 --> 24:40.854
I see!

24:41.396 --> 24:44.107
So this is what "slimy" means.

24:45.192 --> 24:47.277
That's been bothering me.

24:48.278 --> 24:51.698
Sorry, can I take a video?

24:52.282 --> 24:53.575
Yes, of course.

24:54.701 --> 24:56.953
It might help me with my assignment.

24:58.496 --> 25:02.167
I'm in graduate school,
majoring in animation.

25:02.250 --> 25:03.835
Animation?

25:04.419 --> 25:05.795
That's cool.

25:07.464 --> 25:09.883
I'm pursuing my dream.

25:11.176 --> 25:13.720
What's your dream, Taiga?

25:13.803 --> 25:14.804
What?

25:16.014 --> 25:19.309
I like to hear about
other people's dreams.

25:21.645 --> 25:25.190
I don't have a dream.

25:26.149 --> 25:30.320
I'm only working here because I started
as a part-timer and never left.

25:31.029 --> 25:33.865
So you're in training.

25:34.616 --> 25:36.618
Just like me.

25:38.954 --> 25:40.372
Let's do our best.

25:41.373 --> 25:42.415
You can do it!

25:47.254 --> 25:48.338
Oh, that's it.

25:48.421 --> 25:51.466
Can you make a dish that even Koreans

25:51.549 --> 25:53.760
who don't like slimy textures would enjoy?

25:55.011 --> 25:57.973
That's a pretty tall order.

25:58.056 --> 26:01.685
Oh, you will be able to do it, Taiga.

26:01.768 --> 26:04.271
You're able to make
such delicious onigiri, after all.

26:07.107 --> 26:08.358
It'll be fine.

26:09.567 --> 26:10.527
I'm sure.

26:22.038 --> 26:24.833
Okay. I'll give it a try.

26:30.839 --> 26:32.173
Korean pancake with natto.

26:47.063 --> 26:49.065
Bibim-guksu with mekabu seaweed.

27:15.008 --> 27:17.677
Okra wrapped in samgyeopsal.

27:29.981 --> 27:31.566
Thank you for the food.

27:36.571 --> 27:37.947
I'm stuffed.

27:38.656 --> 27:41.284
Thank you for today.

27:42.118 --> 27:44.454
I have a good idea of what to do now.

27:45.455 --> 27:47.582
No, thank you.

27:49.250 --> 27:52.712
Make sure you let me know
when you've perfected the dish.

27:52.796 --> 27:53.713
Yes.

28:02.555 --> 28:06.935
In Korea, you add your own contact info
into the other person's phone.

28:38.675 --> 28:41.678
I need to take out the trash
before I leave.

28:45.598 --> 28:48.601
Okay. Bye then.

29:28.600 --> 29:32.061
Want to go to that
makgeolli place we went to last time?

29:32.771 --> 29:35.482
Sorry, I already ate.

29:36.524 --> 29:37.442
Oh really?

29:37.525 --> 29:39.736
Well, since I'm here,
I'll give you a ride home.

29:42.030 --> 29:42.864
‎Let's go.

30:30.078 --> 30:30.912
It's good.

30:32.372 --> 30:35.792
-I'm impressed, Taiga.
-Thank you.

30:37.961 --> 30:43.550
But for our customers, we might want
to bring down the spiciness a little bit.

30:44.843 --> 30:46.553
Okay, I'll try that.

30:51.516 --> 30:52.350
SECOND WOMEN'S DORM

30:52.433 --> 30:54.894
It's already been a week,

30:55.728 --> 30:58.606
and I still haven't received any word.

30:59.607 --> 31:01.526
I told you, "Don't think about it."

31:02.819 --> 31:04.362
Japanese men

31:04.445 --> 31:08.366
don't contact you
unless there is a reason to.

31:09.450 --> 31:13.997
Well then, how are you supposed to
get to know them better?

31:15.582 --> 31:19.085
You'll just have to take your time
with this one.

31:21.087 --> 31:23.548
It may take at least half a year.

31:24.340 --> 31:25.508
Half a year?

31:29.095 --> 31:30.847
Who is it? Onigiri Man?

31:31.890 --> 31:34.893
KAEDE REAL ESTATE

31:50.700 --> 31:56.831
HELLO, RIN
THANKS TO YOU, OUR NEW MENU ITEM IS SET

32:06.424 --> 32:09.802
RIN - HOW ARE YOU DOING?

32:22.190 --> 32:23.107
Taiga,

32:23.191 --> 32:25.735
sorry for contacting you out of the blue.

32:26.319 --> 32:28.613
No problem,
I was just leaving work anyway.

32:29.781 --> 32:30.782
Also…

32:32.033 --> 32:34.327
-I'm doing good.
-Huh?

32:35.536 --> 32:37.372
Oh, I'm glad.

32:38.039 --> 32:39.874
But… um…

32:40.541 --> 32:43.795
I didn't hear from you, so I was worried.

32:45.713 --> 32:46.673
I'm sorry.

32:47.340 --> 32:50.927
It was officially added to the menu today,

32:51.010 --> 32:53.721
-so I was going to contact you--
-That's not what I mean.

32:54.222 --> 32:58.059
I mean keeping in touch
about normal, ordinary stuff.

33:00.311 --> 33:02.814
Normal, ordinary stuff?

33:04.023 --> 33:07.527
Sharing things about your everyday life,

33:08.152 --> 33:10.822
like what you saw and what you ate.

33:12.699 --> 33:14.909
In order to get to know each other.

33:18.955 --> 33:19.872
But…

33:21.332 --> 33:24.836
wouldn't that make your boyfriend upset?

33:25.545 --> 33:26.587
Boyfriend?

33:28.172 --> 33:29.257
The other day,

33:30.174 --> 33:33.428
he came to pick you up from the restaurant
in his car.

33:35.847 --> 33:37.390
Jun-ho!

33:37.473 --> 33:40.560
He's just a friend.
I don't have a boyfriend!

33:50.903 --> 33:55.408
Taiga, do you have a girlfriend?

34:00.913 --> 34:01.998
No, I don't.

34:09.714 --> 34:10.673
Rain…

34:15.803 --> 34:18.931
-Let's run and find some shelter.
-Okay.

34:58.054 --> 34:59.138
It's like The Classic.

35:01.557 --> 35:02.767
The Classic.

35:03.476 --> 35:07.230
This is like a scene
out of my favorite movie.

35:36.342 --> 35:37.760
Wow!

36:03.578 --> 36:04.787
Please, use this.

36:24.682 --> 36:26.767
No, it's just… It's been a while

36:27.351 --> 36:29.020
since I used a handkerchief.

36:30.271 --> 36:31.689
Thank you.

36:43.117 --> 36:46.829
It's strange…
I was feeling down just a minute ago,

36:47.538 --> 36:51.459
but after running in the rain,
I feel much better.

36:54.670 --> 36:56.923
Something's making you feel down?

37:02.011 --> 37:04.847
Right now, I'm searching
for a new place to live, but…

37:06.807 --> 37:08.434
my application was rejected.

37:17.944 --> 37:20.780
When I messaged you, "How are you doing?"

37:21.530 --> 37:22.531
I think

37:24.033 --> 37:26.994
I was subconsciously asking myself that.

37:34.418 --> 37:36.671
But I can't give up.

37:37.380 --> 37:40.424
Because I want to stay in Japan
a little while longer.

37:48.891 --> 37:49.892
Um…

38:00.069 --> 38:02.405
Sorry, what were you saying?

38:05.783 --> 38:07.493
Can I help you search?

38:08.911 --> 38:09.787
What?

38:11.914 --> 38:13.082
If you…

38:14.000 --> 38:15.042
‎don't mind.

38:28.597 --> 38:30.725
-You are amazing, Rin.
-Amazing?

38:31.517 --> 38:33.060
What about it is amazing?

38:33.144 --> 38:34.395
PREVIEW

38:34.478 --> 38:36.022
When I'm with you,

38:37.273 --> 38:40.401
I feel like I can move forward.

38:40.484 --> 38:42.987
‎THIS DRAMA IS FICTION AND ALL CHARACTERS
‎AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTIONAL

38:43.070 --> 38:43.946
Subtitle translation by: Kiko Morita
